# Phase 27 plan 06 fixture (D-35): a client attaches while a pane is
# needs_input. After the greeting block, the %client-session-changed
# structural notification (a second client attaching to the session)
# drives ONE debounced list-panes re-poll; the test scripts that re-poll's
# Run result with the session's attached count incremented (1 -> 2), which
# must clear needs_input and emit TransitionCleared WITHOUT any pane
# output change (D-04). The greeting deliberately carries no structural
# notification so the only re-poll is the one this fixture's event drives.
<< %begin 1700000000 1 0
<< %end 1700000000 1 0
@delay 600ms
<< %client-session-changed /dev/ttys001 $1 work
# Hold the connection open so steady-state asserts are deterministic; ctx
# cancel ends playback before the line below is ever emitted.
@delay 30s
<< %test-hold-open
